ike the 2008 financial crisis  the european debt crisis and early 2020.  the first reading shows increased fear  in the bond market but is well below  what we would have seen from the index  in 2008 break-even inflation rates have  been sinking in recent weeks even as  inflation readings for this year have  been rising that shows investors expect  inflation will be low in the future even  though it's very high today that  typically signals fears of a recession  because a recession stops growth  bringing down the average rate for  inflation over time the five-year  five-year forward rate is even lower and  recently fell to its lowest rate since  march that suggests longer term growth  expectations are really being decreased  which also signals recession fears and  the treasury yield curve recently  inverted for the second time this year  the yield curve shows investors predict  central banks will need to lower  interest rates in the future that's  usually because a recession has happened  all of these gauges show that investors  are putting more of their bets on a  recession or at least a significant  economic downturn but that doesn't mean  it's guaranteed to happen  rapper yg made a hit song this year by  telling us that scared money don't make  no money but sometimes it does  that's all for now i'll see you next  time  you
 

